{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And they took all the spoil, etc.</b> This tells that they were fit and righteous, and were not suspected concerning theft to lay hand on the spoil without permission — for it says <b>את כל השלל וגו'</b>, and about them it is explicated in the tradition: ״שִׁנַּיִךְ כְּעֵדֶר הָרְחֵלִים״ etc. (Song of Songs 6:6) — even the men of war among you are all righteous." "<b>Spoil (שלל).</b> These are movable goods of clothing and jewelry." "<b>Plunder (בז).</b> This is plunder of movable goods that are not jewelry." "<b>Captive (מלקוח).</b> Person and beast; and in a place where שְׁבִי is written next to מַלְקוֹחַ, שְׁבִי refers to person and מַלְקוֹחַ to beast."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:24.548674357Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}